# Line endings.
#
# Everything in this repository that a Linux container executes must keep LF, whatever
# the checkout platform does by default. Git stores LF, but a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree -- and `docker build` copies the
# working tree verbatim. A shell script that arrives with CRLF has `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`
# as its shebang, so the kernel looks for an interpreter literally named "bash\r" and the
# container dies with exit 127 and the memorable message:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# These rules pin LF for those files, so a Windows checkout builds the same image as a
# Linux one.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Lockfiles and build output are noisy in diffs and never merged by hand
ui/package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
